<urn:atm:triage:finding/ATM-QA-004-AL9>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "ATM-QA-004-AL9" ;
  triage:title "AL.9 graft outbound write / CLI activation physical-proof rows still 'static/source proof' only, not runtime evidence" ;
  triage:description "Physical proof matrix's atm-graft-write and CLI activation rows are backed only by source/static inspection, not by runtime execution producing recorded transcript/log. These rows require smoke test execution in dedicated worktree per team-lead process. INDEPENDENT REVIEW (quality-mgr, 2026-08-10, integrate/phase-al@fc73d4ec / PR #824): verified via gh pr diff that PR #824 (docs-only, AL9-physical-proof-matrix.md +3/-3, sprint-AL9-physical-proof-ledger-freeze.md +23/-0) changes the CLI local write and graft outbound write rows' disposition text to 'Static/source proof; final-candidate runtime row pending', naming team-lead as owner and the frozen final integrate/phase-al candidate SHA as trigger, and adds the corresponding record requirements (CLI write/activation, graft write/nudge/read/ack transcripts) to the new 'Final integrate/phase-al to develop evidence pass' sprint-doc section. This resolves the unowned/unscheduled aspect of the gap (mirroring ATM-QA-002/003-AL9's resolution) but does NOT close this finding: the core defect -- no runtime-executed evidence exists for these two write paths, only static/source proof -- remains genuinely true at fc73d4ec. Per the user's standing constraint ('we are not running another smoke-test until final integration -> develop review occurs'), no new smoke test may be executed right now to close this; it correctly stays open, gated to the same final evidence-pass window as ATM-QA-002-AL9's M5 row. Remains open pending that execution." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-al" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "requirements-completeness" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-08-12T06:15:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:closureNote "Reconciled by arch-ctm's FIX-AL9-AM-RECONCILIATION-1 (docs/al9-am-evidence-reconciliation PR #861, commit 4c0c1d68). CLI-local-write and graft-outbound-write rows in AL9-physical-proof-matrix.md now read Satisfied, citing am6-closure-proof.md's dynamic-evidence table (120-case M5<->M4 crosshost smoke, real message IDs) and two live ATM message receipts documenting a post-daemon-cycle native atm_send retry success plus ack pending-state clearance. quality-mgr independently confirmed the smoke-report artifact exists on disk with the exact case count claimed, and independently confirmed the two cited ATM message IDs (01KZSSSG878QYFGBJVDWTJHXKG, 01KZSVA533HB2XG0YN2X4NB97G) are genuine by querying the raw mail.db directly (not visible via atm read due to mailbox-scoping, since they're addressed to arch-ctm). Windows physical proof row honestly reframed as an explicit Phase AP deferral (VPN/DNS reachability constraint), not a false completion claim. Independently re-confirmed by 4 reviewers this round (req-qa, arch-qa, ruthless-boundary-qa, and quality-mgr's own checks) at commit 2cdedd4d." ;
